                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.002/149: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-13T10:00:00+03:00">April 13, 1941—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. Foreign Office telegraphed [<hi rendition="#italic">telephoned?</hi>] today
                    saying Minister for Foreign Affairs would receive visits of congratulations from
                    chiefs of diplomatic missions tomorrow morning. British, Turkish, Egyptian,
                    Iranian, French and American will not attend leaving only the Japanese and
                    Italian.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
